{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7dbdhfdplf6ngiatshrcwmildhwmlaoxb5qbbenjlk4p5dhkjn3a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`c_src` is untouched (mtimes predate the session; only the generated `build/` was added). Verification complete.\n\n## What I did\n\n**Phase A — mapped the surface** into three artifacts derived mechanically from the C source and `nm -D`/`objdump`:\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — all 22 exported symbols; diff against the Rust `.so` was already empty, so no module was missing.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 44 rows, one per distinct rejection the C actually performs (there are no `assert`s, error enums, or null checks — it rejects purely via `int` returns and ordered float comparisons).\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 62 rows over the axes the C branches on, including a NaN-payload axis I only discovered was necessary later.\n\nThe key move was disassembling the reference build (`-O0`, gcc 11.5) and checking the Rust **instruction for instruction**, since the existing translation used inline `asm!` to pin SSE operand order.\n\n**Phases B–D — 89 differential tests**, all loading both `.so`s via `libloading` and comparing bit-exactly, with out-params pre-filled with a sentinel so \"did it write on the reject path?\" is compared too.\n\n## Bugs found and fixed\n\nEight `mulss`/`addss` **operand-order** errors. These matter because the instruction returns the *destination* operand when both operands are NaN, and gcc's `-O0` destination choice is not the source-order-obvious one — e.g. `c2Dot`'s y-lane product uses `b.y` as destination and the sum uses the *y* product, not the x one. The exported `c2Add`/`c2MulmvT` wrappers also had hand-written bodies that disagreed with the internal helpers the rest of the library calls; they now delegate.\n\nSeparately, `c2CastRay` has no `default:` and no trailing `return`. The old code returned `B as u32`; probing showed the C actually returns `0x249bd63c` while `B`'s low half was `0x245fe350` — it returns its **leftover `%eax`**, which rustc's `call *%rax` sets to the callee's own address. I replaced the export with a `#[unsafe(naked)]` stub (`cmp esi, 2; ja 2f; jmp dispatch; 2: ret`) that reproduces the C's instruction semantics exactly.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n**I wrote a mutation checker to test my own tests**, and it exposed a real blind spot: my first suite killed only 17 of 22 injected bugs. The cause was that reusing one `f32::NAN` value can never reveal operand order — you need *distinct* payloads. Adding `phase_b_nan_payloads.rs` (48 mutually distinguishable NaNs at varying densities) took it to 49/58 killed, and it's what catches fixes #6–#8. Every remaining survivor is a proven-**equivalent** mutant with a reachability argument recorded in the script (e.g. `out->t` in the `t0`/`t1`/`t2` AABB branches can't see two NaNs, because taking those branches requires `t0 >= t1 && ...`, which is false for NaN — and the `t3` branch mutant *is* killed, proving the site is genuinely exercised).\n\n**One residual difference is unfixable, and I want to be explicit rather than claim full parity.** For an out-of-range `typeB`, if the caller uses `call *%rax`, the C returns its own address and the Rust returns its own — different values. No translation can fix that; it's the caller's `%eax` leaking through genuine UB. So `err_38` asserts what *can* hold: `*out` untouched in both, `B` never dereferenced, and each returning its incoming `%eax` (verified against the entry addresses). That's a real equality — a mutant returning `0` is caught — but it is not byte-identical returns in every calling convention.\n\nAlso worth noting: I matched the `-O0` build the task's cmake command produces. At `-O2` gcc may vectorise the lanes, which could shift NaN payload selection (never ordinary values — gcc doesn't reassociate FP without `-ffast-math`, and baseline x86-64 has no FMA).\n\n`./run_all.sh` runs everything across both profiles × both feature combos (`Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`, so that's the whole cross-product) and exits 0."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_read_input_tokens":324096,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":915,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20cfd266-ad25-4bd4-8d50-d08897c4517a","uuid":"56fe7fd9-c322-433f-955a-c8445857d416","timestamp":"2026-08-27T08:54:14.775Z"}
